        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-400",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing Maximum Length Constraint on Menu Item Search Query Parameter\n\nThe staff-facing menu search endpoint accepts a query string parameter `q` with no upper-length bound. The application compiles this unbounded input into a JavaScript `RegExp` object before passing it to MongoDB, enabling authenticated staff members to submit arbitrarily large strings that cause disproportionate CPU and memory consumption on both the API server and the database node."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.routes.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 61,
                  "endLine": 62,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const searchSchema = z.object({ q: z.string().min(1) })"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Add max() constraint to search schema"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/v1/app/menu/items/search",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.routes.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 61,
                        "endLine": 62
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "const searchSchema = z.object({ q: z.string().min(1).max(200) })"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Add a maximum length constraint to the search schema so that the query string is rejected at the validation layer before any regex or database operation is performed. A limit of 200 characters is consistent with the `reason` field in transition schemas and is more than sufficient for real menu searches. Additionally, consider enforcing a maximum regex pattern size at the `searchItems` service level as defence-in-depth.",
                "markdown": "Add a maximum length constraint to the search schema so that the query string is rejected at the validation layer before any regex or database operation is performed. A limit of 200 characters is consistent with the `reason` field in transition schemas and is more than sufficient for real menu searches. Additionally, consider enforcing a maximum regex pattern size at the `searchItems` service level as defence-in-depth."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "73f172240f4519132cb3fc628d6d5a312ad5f77b1b09be0881250c877f6c8d47"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "4.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "e372ee155a1acad80a0309ccb66b67cd8d325c2beca4c80050b2d6663a035241",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0002",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 4.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-19 10:18:47 UTC",
              "target": "Restaurant Webapp — `apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.routes.ts`, `apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.service.ts`",
              "endpoint": "/api/v1/app/menu/items/search",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-400",
              "impact": "An authenticated staff member (any role that can access the menu — WAITER, CASHIER, KITCHEN, MANAGER, OWNER) can submit a very long query string (e.g., hundreds of kilobytes) to the search endpoint. The API server executes `new RegExp(largeString, 'i')` and then issues a MongoDB `$regex` query against four indexed fields. This can cause elevated CPU usage, slow query execution, or service degradation for other users of the same API process. The attack requires valid staff credentials.",
              "technical_analysis": "In `menu.routes.ts`, the query schema is:\n\n```typescript title=apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.routes.ts startLineNumber=61 endLineNumber=62\nconst searchSchema = z.object({ q: z.string().min(1) })\n```\n\nNo `.max()` is applied. The validated value is passed to `menuService.searchItems()`:\n\n```typescript title=apps/api/src/modules/menu/menu.service.ts startLineNumber=235 endLineNumber=244\nexport async function searchItems(query: string): Promise<MenuItemView[]> {\n  const repo = tenantRepo(MenuItemModel)\n  const safeQuery = query.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&')\n  const regex = new RegExp(safeQuery, 'i')\n\n  const items = await repo.find({\n    $or: [\n      { 'name.en': { $regex: regex } },\n      { 'name.ar': { $regex: regex } },\n      { 'description.en': { $regex: regex } },\n      { 'description.ar': { $regex: regex } }\n    ]\n  }, { limit: 50 })\n\n  return items.map(toItemView)\n}\n```\n\nThe metacharacter escaping neutralizes catastrophic-backtracking patterns (the `[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]` substitution is correct), but there is no bound on the resulting string length before it is compiled into a `RegExp`. A 500 KB query string becomes a 500 KB regex pattern object in memory and a 500 KB BSON `$regex` clause sent to MongoDB. The global JSON body limit (`BODY_LIMIT=100kb`) only applies to request bodies — query strings bypass it. The general `apiRateLimit` (300 req/min) limits how many such requests can be made but does not restrict the size of each individual request.",
              "remediation_steps": "Add a maximum length constraint to the search schema so that the query string is rejected at the validation layer before any regex or database operation is performed. A limit of 200 characters is consistent with the `reason` field in transition schemas and is more than sufficient for real menu searches. Additionally, consider enforcing a maximum regex pattern size at the `searchItems` service level as defence-in-depth.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Authenticate as any staff member (WAITER or higher role) and obtain a valid access token.\n2. Construct a GET request to `/api/v1/app/menu/items/search` with a `q` parameter containing a very long string (e.g., 100,000 repetitions of `a`).\n3. Observe that the server processes the request without rejecting it for size.\n4. Monitor server CPU and response latency; both increase proportionally to the query string length.\n5. Repeat at the rate limit (300/min) to sustain elevated load.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-863",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing `REFUNDED` Guard in `confirmCashPayment` Allows Payment Status Manipulation After Refund\n\nThe `confirmCashPayment` function in `order.service.ts` only guards against re-payment when `paymentStatus === PAID`. It does not guard against `paymentStatus === REFUNDED`, so a cashier who issues a refund can immediately call the cash-confirmation endpoint again to silently flip the payment status back to `PAID` — effectively erasing the refund from the live record without any audit trail."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/orders/order.service.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 633,
                  "endLine": 637,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "if (order.paymentStatus === PaymentStatus.PAID) {\n    // Idempotent from the cashier's point of view: a double-click reports the\n    // truth rather than double-recording a payment.\n    throw conflict('This order is already paid')\n  }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Missing REFUNDED guard — primary fix location"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/orders/order.service.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 649,
                  "endLine": 666,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const updated = await repo.findOneAndUpdate(\n    { _id: order._id, paymentStatus: order.paymentStatus },\n    { $set: { paymentStatus: PaymentStatus.PAID } },\n    { new: true }\n  )\n  \n  if (!updated) {\n    throw conflict('This order was changed by someone else. Refresh and try again.')\n  }\n  \n  try {\n    const { getIO } = await import('../../core/socket.js')\n    getIO().to(`restaurant_${updated.restaurantId}`).emit('order_updated')\n  } catch (err) {\n    logger.warn({ err }, 'failed to emit order_updated')\n  }\n  \n  return toOrderView(updated)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Missing writeAudit in kitchenStartsBeforePayment path — secondary fix"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/orders/:id/confirm-cash",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/orders/order.service.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 633,
                        "endLine": 637
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "if (order.paymentStatus === PaymentStatus.PAID) {\n    // Idempotent from the cashier's point of view: a double-click reports the\n    // truth rather than double-recording a payment.\n    throw conflict('This order is already paid')\n  }\n  if (order.paymentStatus === PaymentStatus.REFUNDED) {\n    throw conflict('This order has been refunded and cannot be re-confirmed as paid')\n  }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "apps/api/src/modules/orders/order.service.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 649,
                        "endLine": 666
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "const updated = await repo.findOneAndUpdate(\n    { _id: order._id, paymentStatus: order.paymentStatus },\n    { $set: { paymentStatus: PaymentStatus.PAID } },\n    { new: true }\n  )\n  \n  if (!updated) {\n    throw conflict('This order was changed by someone else. Refresh and try again.')\n  }\n\n  await writeAudit({\n    action: AuditAction.CASH_CONFIRMED,\n    targetType: 'Order',\n    targetId: order._id.toString(),\n    metadata: {\n      orderNumber: order.orderNumber,\n      grandTotalHalalas: order.totals?.grandTotalHalalas,\n    },\n  })\n\n  try {\n    const { getIO } = await import('../../core/socket.js')\n    getIO().to(`restaurant_${updated.restaurantId}`).emit('order_updated')\n  } catch (err) {\n    logger.warn({ err }, 'failed to emit order_updated')\n  }\n  \n  return toOrderView(updated)"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Add an explicit guard for `PaymentStatus.REFUNDED` immediately after the existing `PAID` guard in `confirmCashPayment`. A refunded order represents a completed financial reversal; re-confirming it as paid must be rejected with a clear error, just as a double-payment is rejected today. Additionally, the non-`CASH_PENDING` branch of `confirmCashPayment` should call `writeAudit` with `AuditAction.CASH_CONFIRMED` so that every successful cash confirmation — including in `kitchenStartsBeforePayment = true` mode — is captured in the audit log, matching the behavior of the `transitionOrder` path.",
                "markdown": "Add an explicit guard for `PaymentStatus.REFUNDED` immediately after the existing `PAID` guard in `confirmCashPayment`. A refunded order represents a completed financial reversal; re-confirming it as paid must be rejected with a clear error, just as a double-payment is rejected today. Additionally, the non-`CASH_PENDING` branch of `confirmCashPayment` should call `writeAudit` with `AuditAction.CASH_CONFIRMED` so that every successful cash confirmation — including in `kitchenStartsBeforePayment = true` mode — is captured in the audit log, matching the behavior of the `transitionOrder` path."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "6bfcfe465f5cc771a432cf167601a6ab0ec625693e02df99f2abb6ce7ab90fe7"
